       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. Doses that high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. They don't add meaningful analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nSome common regimens you may have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day. This is a typical analgesic dose.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day. This is often used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, usually for short-term use with monitoring.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter it once you do. Taking ibuprofen with food and using the lowest effective dose for the shortest time are standard precautions."
      }
